## 6. Proof-of-Work Consensus

Bitcoin uses proof-of-work as part of its consensus mechanism.

Miners compete to produce blocks that satisfy the network's proof-of-work requirements. Nodes independently validate proposed blocks and transactions before accepting them into their view of the blockchain.

Proof-of-work contributes to Bitcoin's resistance to unauthorized rewriting of transaction history.

From an infrastructure perspective, this introduces several important concepts:

- Mining
- Hashing
- Difficulty
- Block production
- Chain selection
- Network propagation
- Economic incentives
- Computational security

