## 8. Wallets and Key Management

A Bitcoin wallet does not literally store bitcoin.

The blockchain records transactions and unspent outputs. Wallet software manages the cryptographic keys needed to authorize transactions and helps users interact with those blockchain records.

Important security concepts include:

- Private keys
- Public keys
- Seed phrases
- Wallet backups
- Hardware wallets
- Software wallets
- Multisignature authorization
- Transaction signing
- Secure key storage

The security of the private-key environment is therefore fundamental to digital-asset security.

